{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730119Z","id":"6c8263c15b4e53e447a913833b9f54feebc1208cb582a2b082a0d920ca3608ac","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:115 (Q2)): sandboxed Grok is unsupported unless a daemon already runs; under the workspace, read-only and strict profiles a daemon the shim starts cannot write ~/.clax (docs/contract.md:4203-4207). Supporting it needs sandbox detection in the shim and a daemon start outside the sandbox; the contract's Known-limitations entry then goes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":185},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"640b44f0e9381845d6a718e1018b787e83435bdbaa898535326273c8c39a837e"},"summary":"Support Grok's sandbox: detect it in the shim and start the daemon outside it","tags":["revisit:Grok users run with the sandbox on and no daemon started outside it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:29:45.207442Z","id":"038844cbfbf4e93c7ee1ab9b9872d06464c08dc181ebba1142ea5010aff757c3","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:115 (Q2)): sandboxed Grok is unsupported unless a daemon already runs; under the workspace, read-only and strict profiles a daemon the shim starts cannot write ~/.clax (docs/contract.md:4203-4207). Supporting it needs sandbox detection in the shim and a daemon start outside the sandbox; the contract's Known-limitations entry then goes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":190},"end":{"line":198},"content_hash":"d9959f5d584066d4e69e140993450c2f50d43d874d097d9bac813fe993476b6a"},"summary":"Support Grok's sandbox: detect it in the shim and start the daemon outside it","supersedes":"6c8263c15b4e53e447a913833b9f54feebc1208cb582a2b082a0d920ca3608ac","tags":["revisit:Grok users run with the sandbox on and no daemon started outside it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619083Z","id":"7b5749bd659189973546d590ce7735c100bcab247f10b10d99fc6fae4018ce9e","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:115 (Q2)): sandboxed Grok is unsupported unless a daemon already runs; under the workspace, read-only and strict profiles a daemon the shim starts cannot write ~/.clax (docs/contract.md:4203-4207). Supporting it needs sandbox detection in the shim and a daemon start outside the sandbox; the contract's Known-limitations entry then goes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":198},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"d9959f5d584066d4e69e140993450c2f50d43d874d097d9bac813fe993476b6a"},"summary":"Support Grok's sandbox: detect it in the shim and start the daemon outside it","supersedes":"038844cbfbf4e93c7ee1ab9b9872d06464c08dc181ebba1142ea5010aff757c3","tags":["revisit:Grok users run with the sandbox on and no daemon started outside it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.889533Z","id":"8bd3a5dd80c39c3894d638d0d133c7b5d69653c3624ef606ea9bccdf08f95e67","body":{"detail":"A withheld anchor's file is null in the thread view (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs placeholder::anchor, spec §8.3), and comments_read maps a null file to INDEX_FILE here, so the agent is told the thread is on index.html. No withheld text leaks; the file it names may be wrong. The shim's view of withheld fields (anchor_withheld, clip_withheld, withheld) is not formatted yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":567},"end":{"line":567},"content_hash":"1c7991c30f6eeaff531e82713cb230c0447e5b7f4ea8affd5c54ab6e58c9b6d7"},"suggested_fix":"When the thread is anchor_withheld, give file null (or say the anchor is withheld) and carry the withheld summary into the tool result, with the rest of the tiers' filtering.","summary":"comments_read shows a withheld anchor's file as index.html","tags":["visibility","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.795162Z","id":"b7f24ef98974dfb949341d6ba66f1baa4ec194e102ab719ddd9ad6ef430949f5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f44be2c","summary":"Fixed: thread_summary gives a withheld anchor no file and no summary and carries anchor_withheld, clip_withheld, each comment's withheld flag and the thread's withheld summary. Test: cargo test -p clax-mcp --lib a_thread_summary_keeps_withheld_fields_withheld passes; api_visibility::mcp_tools_are_filtered_for_the_owner passes.","supersedes":"8bd3a5dd80c39c3894d638d0d133c7b5d69653c3624ef606ea9bccdf08f95e67","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:45:51.492804Z","id":"4b4a862fbd01266f56a6471c08566fb80ed3d8978c867fedae8cbbb97479fba8","body":{"detail":"Failure: a remote daemon puts clip_path \"/Users/sam/.clax/remote.key\" (or ~/.ssh/id_ed25519) on a thread; comments_read and the feedback payload's `Clip:` line hand it to the agent, whose tool description says to view the clip with its file tools, so the agent reads a local secret into its context. A daemon serving a grant never sends clip_path (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:520 only with the token), so any path from a remote daemon is foreign. Plan Task 19 rewrites remote clip lines to cached files.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":585},"end":{"line":610},"content_hash":"e5ad9f7463b428b2b184731654cc20f56c86793209b057a750f70798b912f9bc"},"suggested_fix":"In Task 19's rewrite, never pass a remote clip_path or snapshot_path through: replace it with the fetched file under <home>/remote-cache/clips/ or `Clip: unavailable (…)`.","summary":"In remote mode the agent is shown whatever clip path the remote daemon sends, as a file to open","tags":["security","review","revisit:Task 19 remote clip rewrite","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T16:50:12.003938Z","id":"09424caedb6427bd7d18c7e2095a0865f3a3ea75ddb2f00e6f6df2f174650d79","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:115 (Q2)): sandboxed Grok is unsupported unless a daemon already runs; under the workspace, read-only and strict profiles a daemon the shim starts cannot write ~/.clax (docs/contract.md:4203-4207). Supporting it needs sandbox detection in the shim and a daemon start outside the sandbox; the contract's Known-limitations entry then goes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":201},"end":{"line":218},"content_hash":"8ad74131cff0e96c44a667e6a3d7aecd30ec5c516b2e0c49d35a42face7a17c9"},"summary":"Support Grok's sandbox: detect it in the shim and start the daemon outside it","supersedes":"7b5749bd659189973546d590ce7735c100bcab247f10b10d99fc6fae4018ce9e","tags":["revisit:Grok users run with the sandbox on and no daemon started outside it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.638636Z","id":"03903a98e24585272ee2c89f8e32daf0dbf0883252391991ca464ea98da6f7a6","body":{"detail":"Failure: a shim holds session X (or finds X in its file), and the remote daemon has no row X (the machine reconnected to another daemon without clax connect --off, or the daemon's data was reset). The registration with X is 400 unknown_session from Identity::caller's own_session check, which is not proof_refused, so the loop returns the error without trying the file or no credential; every later call refreshes and fails the same way until the shim restarts. The SessionStart hook's join (crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs:459-476) stops the same way on a stale file from another daemon.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":530},"end":{"line":540},"content_hash":"502da82e4cf94e5e61dbd9f953d24bd305aed30374e33fc6fb08b0eb3ca77039"},"suggested_fix":"Treat 400 unknown_session like invalid_session_proof when choosing the next registration or join candidate.","summary":"A registration whose held or filed credential names a session the daemon does not know stops instead of trying the next candidate","tags":["review","spec:6.8","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:20.902153Z","id":"299bddff81cc21828b327be9e964a7bbc071cac5474f9d1ed828a540e38ce6c0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:903f2670","summary":"The shim's registration and the hook's join pass over a credential refused as 400 unknown_session as they do one refused as invalid_session_proof (credential_refused). Evidence: remote::a_credential_for_a_session_the_daemon_does_not_know_is_passed_over and hook::join_tests::a_found_credential_is_used_and_a_stale_one_dropped pass; the mutation dropping unknown_session is caught.","supersedes":"03903a98e24585272ee2c89f8e32daf0dbf0883252391991ca464ea98da6f7a6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.743099Z","id":"aa30ce24a864109463092446a5f07afc629e74d95195bfcf72fe4ed824217718","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"A grant session's payload names its clip clax-clip:<artifact>/<thread>; the shim, hooks and Pi fetch it into <home>/remote-cache/clips/ and rewrite the line, and any other Clip: or Snapshot: value and any clip_path or snapshot_path from a remote daemon becomes unavailable or null (clax_core::clips). Evidence: clips::tests::*, remote::remote_clip_lines_are_rewritten_to_cached_files and connect::remote_hooks_find_their_session pass; the shim test fails with the rewrite off.","supersedes":"4b4a862fbd01266f56a6471c08566fb80ed3d8978c867fedae8cbbb97479fba8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.319529Z","id":"6a33fedc3bc1f05db65d1e8b67287da978958c8e5caf01876efe48f5ca71c666","body":{"detail":"clip_bytes here, Client::get_bytes_with (crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:978-989) and Pi's DaemonClient.clipBytes (plugins/pi/src/client.ts) buffer the whole response, and clax_core::clips::store / Pi's storeClip write it to <home>/remote-cache/clips/<aid>-<tid>.png. clips.rs treats a remote daemon as untrusted for paths (it never passes one through), but a hostile or broken daemon can answer a clip GET with gigabytes: the shim, hook or Pi process grows until it is killed and fills the cache disk. Content-Type is not checked, so any bytes are handed to the agent's file tools as an image.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1169},"end":{"line":1180},"content_hash":"6e5f63621aa4954611320f7c927134ad3280706fd154357768d939fefac6c157"},"suggested_fix":"Cap the body (the daemon's own clip upload limit is the natural bound), refuse a non-image/png Content-Type, and rewrite either to `Clip: unavailable (…)`.","summary":"Remote clips are read whole into memory with no size cap and stored as .png whatever their type, in the shim, the hooks and Pi","tags":["review","remote","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.319836Z","id":"e65e38868bca2de84279061ea4b09db817850b300eb5e3ffc578faff16b202b1","body":{"detail":"The daemon route is POST /api/sessions/<sid>/threads/<tid>/handoff and takes no artifact. An agent that passes artifact A with a thread ID from artifact B hands off B's thread and is answered {artifact_id: A, url: A's URL, thread: B's}. Pi's commentsHandoff (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts) does the same.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1600},"end":{"line":1627},"content_hash":"c323ff5b1c677601b0c220be54d5fe9469799088faba395f8358f6ca05d27e09"},"suggested_fix":"Check that the returned thread's artifact is the resolved one (400 invalid_args otherwise), or report the thread's own artifact.","summary":"comments_handoff resolves url_or_id but sends only the thread ID, so the result can name an artifact the thread is not on","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.443571Z","id":"0675d7aad833ea9466808918f2855b128fdbfec4bcdefb0330c4b3f80b1d305e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"Clip bodies are read to at most clax_core::clips::MAX_BYTES (+1) and must be image/png with a PNG signature before they are stored, in the shim (chunked read), the hook (Client::get_bytes_with streaming with a cap) and Pi (maxBytes, checkClip). Evidence: clips::tests::a_clip_is_checked_before_it_is_kept and Pi's 'a clip that does not come in time, or is not a PNG ...' (Clip: unavailable (not a PNG)) pass. A signed remote response is still read under the transport's 128 MiB cap before the clip check in the shim.","supersedes":"6a33fedc3bc1f05db65d1e8b67287da978958c8e5caf01876efe48f5ca71c666","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.445771Z","id":"ef7f194e70806d8c8da11284003348631217a29e0b814cbb922fe386635cbab3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"comments_handoff first reads the thread on the named artifact (404 not_found otherwise), in the Rust tools and Pi. Evidence: people::comments_handoff_moves_and_releases and Pi's 'comments_handoff hands a thread to another agent by name and releases it' pass with a wrong-artifact case; without the read the Rust test fails.","supersedes":"e65e38868bca2de84279061ea4b09db817850b300eb5e3ffc578faff16b202b1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
